From c686821bea8038536f6c04d2b3e1baf09aaee0eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:48:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] clk: meson: add Amlogic T7 peripherals clock controller

Add a driver for the T7 (A311D2) peripherals clock controller covering
the system clock gates, the SD/eMMC composite clocks and the Ethernet
RMII/125M clocks. Register offsets and bit positions follow the Linux
t7-peripherals driver.

The fixed PLL, the fdivX dividers and the sys clock are owned by the SCP
firmware on T7 and are taken as external inputs from the device tree.
The driver is only built for MESON_T7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
